  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/19D99C">Notation <span data-tag="19D99C">3.2.2.3</span>.</a> Let $\phi : A^0 \leftarrow \ldots \leftarrow A^ n$ be a composable sequence of maps of simplicial sets. To give an edge $e$ of $M(\phi )$, one must give a pair of integers $0 \leq i \leq j \leq n$ and an edge $\overline{e} \in A^{j}$. We will say that $e$ is <em>marked</em> if $\overline{e}$ is degenerate; let $\calE $ denote the set of all marked edges of $M(\phi )$. Then the pair $(M(\phi ), \calE )$ is a marked simplicial set which we will denote by $M^{\natural }(\phi )$.mapping simplex!markedMnatphi@$M^{\natural }(\phi )$ </p>
